    fix(speckit): the withdrawal is a no-answer path, and the constitution decides too
    
    Three findings from the review on #350, all confirmed against the skills they
    are about.
    
    The withdrawal rule was made unconditional in the last commit, on the reasoning
    that an answer the repository cannot derive is one the spec should have carried.
    The reasoning holds and the conclusion did not. Step 4 exists to put exactly
    those questions to a person, so unattended it withdrew and attended it took the
    question away from the only reader who could close it — with the trigger this
    whole section names, a pause reached with no answer, never having happened. The
    question is put like any other now and withdrawn only when nothing comes back,
    which also restores the sentence the last commit had to weaken.
    
    The in-scope test counted the three artifacts and this feature's design records
    as prior deciders and left out the constitution. A conflict with a constitution
    MUST is automatically CRITICAL, and `speckit-analyze` says in its own words that
    it requires adjusting the spec, plan or tasks rather than diluting or ignoring
    the principle. Bringing a drifted artifact back into line decides nothing — the
    constitution decided it — but under the old condition 2 that fix read as out of
    scope and got filed. `_predicates.analyze` reads the report's existence, so
    `implement` would then have run over a known CRITICAL: the one class of finding
    the skill refuses to let stand, filed by the policy that was supposed to settle
    it.
    
    And the second outcome was stated absolutely — "every other finding is filed" —
    and qualified three paragraphs later, which is the third time this branch has
    shipped that shape. `wfctl issue create` exits 1 on an ungranted branch, which is
    the common case, so a run reading that exit as an action left unfinished has no
    completed state to reach and ends with no scan file. Writing the filing down is
    how that door closes, said where the rule is first stated.
    
    Both P1 fixes carry a test, and one of them asserts the absence of the word the
    last commit introduced.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
